@* Form (UI docs). Sections: Usage, Examples, Customization, Styling reference, API, Accessibility, Guidelines. *@
@* The MVC tag helpers are off on this page: the ui-doc-code snippets show asp-for and a post form as text, and with
   them on, asp-for would be compiled against the docs page's own model. *@
@removeTagHelper *, Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.TagHelpers

<ul class="dnf-docs-source">
    <li>CSS <code>src/DotNetForge.UI/Styles/components/form.css</code></li>
    <li>No tag helper - the classes are the API</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="usage">Usage</h2>
<p>A form is a column of <a href="@UiDocsCatalog.Root/components/field">fields</a>, optionally laid out in a grid, and a row of
    actions at the end. Put <code>dnf-form</code> on the <code>&lt;form&gt;</code>, <code>dnf-form-grid</code> around fields that sit
    side by side and <code>dnf-form-actions</code> around the buttons.</p>

<ui-doc-example id="basic" layout="block">
    <form class="dnf-form dnf-form--narrow" action="#basic">
        <div class="dnf-form-grid">
            <div class="dnf-field">
                <label class="dnf-field__label" for="form-title">Title<span class="dnf-field__required" aria-hidden="true">*</span></label>
                <input class="dnf-input" id="form-title" value="About us" required />
            </div>
            <div class="dnf-field">
                <label class="dnf-field__label" for="form-slug">Slug</label>
                <input class="dnf-input" id="form-slug" value="about-us" />
            </div>
            <div class="dnf-field dnf-form-grid__full">
                <label class="dnf-field__label" for="form-summary">Summary<span class="dnf-field__optional">optional</span></label>
                <textarea class="dnf-textarea" id="form-summary" rows="3" aria-describedby="form-summary-help"></textarea>
                <span class="dnf-field__description" id="form-summary-help">Shown in search results and link previews.</span>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="dnf-form-actions dnf-form-actions--end">
            <button type="button" class="dnf-button dnf-button--secondary">Cancel</button>
            <button type="button" class="dnf-button dnf-button--primary" data-docs-toast="Page saved." data-docs-toast-tone="success">Save</button>
        </div>
    </form>
</ui-doc-example>

<h2 id="examples">Examples</h2>

<ui-doc-example id="stacked" title="Stacked" description="Without a grid the fields stack with the form's own rhythm; dnf-form--narrow caps the width at 44rem." layout="block">
    <form class="dnf-form dnf-form--narrow" action="#stacked">
        <div class="dnf-field">
            <label class="dnf-field__label" for="stacked-name">Site name</label>
            <input class="dnf-input" id="stacked-name" value="DotNetForge" />
        </div>
        <div class="dnf-field">
            <label class="dnf-field__label" for="stacked-email">Contact email</label>
            <input class="dnf-input" id="stacked-email" type="email" value="hello@@example.com" autocomplete="email" />
        </div>
        <div class="dnf-form-actions">
            <button type="button" class="dnf-button dnf-button--primary" data-docs-toast="Settings saved." data-docs-toast-tone="success">Save settings</button>
        </div>
    </form>
</ui-doc-example>

<ui-doc-example id="three-columns" title="Three columns" description="dnf-form-grid--3 for short values; every grid falls back to one column below 40rem." layout="block">
    <form class="dnf-form" action="#three-columns">
        <div class="dnf-form-grid dnf-form-grid--3">
            <div class="dnf-field">
                <label class="dnf-field__label" for="cols-width">Max width</label>
                <input class="dnf-input" id="cols-width" type="number" value="1920" />
            </div>
            <div class="dnf-field">
                <label class="dnf-field__label" for="cols-height">Max height</label>
                <input class="dnf-input" id="cols-height" type="number" value="1080" />
            </div>
            <div class="dnf-field">
                <label class="dnf-field__label" for="cols-quality">Quality</label>
                <input class="dnf-input" id="cols-quality" type="number" value="82" />
            </div>
        </div>
    </form>
</ui-doc-example>

<ui-doc-example id="full-row" title="A field across the grid" description="dnf-form-grid__full on a field spans every column of its grid." layout="block">
    <form class="dnf-form" action="#full-row">
        <div class="dnf-form-grid">
            <div class="dnf-field">
                <label class="dnf-field__label" for="row-first">First name</label>
                <input class="dnf-input" id="row-first" value="Ada" autocomplete="given-name" />
            </div>
            <div class="dnf-field">
                <label class="dnf-field__label" for="row-last">Last name</label>
                <input class="dnf-input" id="row-last" value="Lovelace" autocomplete="family-name" />
            </div>
            <div class="dnf-field dnf-form-grid__full">
                <label class="dnf-field__label" for="row-bio">Biography</label>
                <textarea class="dnf-textarea" id="row-bio" rows="3"></textarea>
            </div>
        </div>
    </form>
</ui-doc-example>

<ui-doc-example id="actions" title="Action row" description="Secondary actions first, the primary one last; dnf-form-actions--end moves the row to the end." layout="stack">
    <div class="dnf-form-actions">
        <button type="button" class="dnf-button dnf-button--primary" data-docs-toast="Webhook saved." data-docs-toast-tone="success">Save webhook</button>
        <button type="button" class="dnf-button dnf-button--secondary" data-docs-toast="Test delivery sent." data-docs-toast-tone="info">Send test</button>
    </div>
    <div class="dnf-form-actions dnf-form-actions--end">
        <button type="button" class="dnf-button dnf-button--ghost">Cancel</button>
        <button type="button" class="dnf-button dnf-button--primary" data-docs-toast="User created." data-docs-toast-tone="success">Create user</button>
    </div>
</ui-doc-example>

<h3 id="server-form">A server form</h3>
<p>A real admin form posts with the antiforgery token, lists the server's errors at the top with
    <a href="@UiDocsCatalog.Root/components/alert">the validation summary</a> and marks its submit button pending while the
    request runs (<code>data-pending-on-submit</code>, see <a href="@UiDocsCatalog.Root/behaviours">behaviours</a>). Destructive
    forms also carry <code>data-confirm</code>.</p>

<ui-doc-code id="server-form-code" lang="razor">
<form method="post" class="dnf-form dnf-form--narrow" data-pending-on-submit>
    @@Html.AntiForgeryToken()
    <dnf-validation-summary />
    <div class="dnf-form-grid">
        <div class="dnf-field">
            <label class="dnf-field__label" asp-for="Title">Title<span class="dnf-field__required" aria-hidden="true">*</span></label>
            <input class="dnf-input" asp-for="Title" required />
            <span class="dnf-field__error" asp-validation-for="Title"></span>
        </div>
        <div class="dnf-field">
            <label class="dnf-field__label" asp-for="Slug">Slug</label>
            <input class="dnf-input" asp-for="Slug" />
            <span class="dnf-field__error" asp-validation-for="Slug"></span>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="dnf-form-actions dnf-form-actions--end">
        <a class="dnf-button dnf-button--secondary" href="/admin/pages">Cancel</a>
        <button type="submit" class="dnf-button dnf-button--primary">Save</button>
    </div>
</form>
</ui-doc-code>

<h2 id="customization">Customization</h2>
<p>The three <a href="@UiDocsCatalog.Root/customization">customization levels</a>, none needing <code>!important</code>. The form
    classes have no component tokens; Level 1 is the modifiers <code>--narrow</code>, <code>--3</code>, <code>__full</code> and
    <code>--end</code>.</p>

<ui-doc-example id="custom-tailwind" title="Tailwind utilities" description="Utilities you add beat the component styles: a four-column grid on large screens, a wider gap." layout="block">
    <form class="dnf-form gap-8" action="#custom-tailwind">
        <div class="dnf-form-grid lg:grid-cols-4">
            <div class="dnf-field">
                <label class="dnf-field__label" for="tw-from">From</label>
                <input class="dnf-input" id="tw-from" type="date" value="2026-01-01" />
            </div>
            <div class="dnf-field">
                <label class="dnf-field__label" for="tw-to">To</label>
                <input class="dnf-input" id="tw-to" type="date" value="2026-01-31" />
            </div>
            <div class="dnf-field">
                <label class="dnf-field__label" for="tw-user">User</label>
                <input class="dnf-input" id="tw-user" value="ada" />
            </div>
            <div class="dnf-field">
                <label class="dnf-field__label" for="tw-action">Action</label>
                <select class="dnf-select" id="tw-action">
                    <option>Any</option>
                    <option>Page published</option>
                    <option>User signed in</option>
                </select>
            </div>
        </div>
    </form>
</ui-doc-example>

<ui-doc-example id="custom-css" title="Your own CSS" description="Unlayered CSS beats every component style - here an uneven grid from 40rem up." layout="block">
    <form class="dnf-form dnf-docs-demo-form" action="#custom-css">
        <div class="dnf-form-grid">
