            </div>
        </div>
    </form>
</ui-doc-example>

<ui-doc-code id="custom-css-code" lang="css">
@@media (min-width: 40rem) {
    .dnf-docs-demo-form .dnf-form-grid { grid-template-columns: 2fr 1fr; }
}
</ui-doc-code>

<h2 id="styling">Styling reference</h2>
<h3 id="classes">Classes</h3>
<table>
    <thead><tr><th>Class</th><th>Kind</th><th>Effect</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-form</code></td><td>block</td><td>a flex column with gap <code>--dnf-space-5</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-form--narrow</code></td><td>modifier</td><td><code>max-width: var(--dnf-form-max)</code> (44rem)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-form-grid</code></td><td>block</td><td>two equal columns, gap <code>--dnf-space-4</code> / <code>--dnf-space-5</code>, fields aligned to the top; one column below 40rem</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-form-grid--3</code></td><td>modifier</td><td>three columns; one below 40rem</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-form-grid__full</code></td><td>element</td><td>a field spanning every column</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-form-actions</code></td><td>block</td><td>a wrapping row of buttons, gap <code>--dnf-space-2</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-form-actions--end</code></td><td>modifier</td><td>the row aligned to the end</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h3 id="states">States</h3>
<p>The form itself has none. Its fields' states (invalid, disabled, read-only) are on the
    <a href="@UiDocsCatalog.Root/components/field#states">field</a> and <a href="@UiDocsCatalog.Root/components/input#states">input</a> pages.</p>

<h2 id="api">API</h2>
<p>There is no tag helper: the classes above are the API. The form takes two behaviour hooks from <code>dnf.js</code>:</p>
<table>
    <thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>On</th><th>Effect</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>data-pending-on-submit</code></td><td><code>&lt;form&gt;</code></td><td>on a submit that was not cancelled, the submitter (else the first submit button) gets <code>data-pending="true"</code> and <code>aria-busy="true"</code> - the button shows its spinner until the next page loads</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>data-confirm</code></td><td><code>&lt;form&gt;</code> or a submit button</td><td>asks in the confirmation dialog before the form is sent, with <code>data-confirm-title</code>, <code>data-confirm-action</code> and <code>data-confirm-tone</code> (<a href="@UiDocsCatalog.Root/behaviours">behaviours</a>)</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>
<p>Server errors go in <code>&lt;dnf-validation-summary /&gt;</code> at the top of the form (<a href="@UiDocsCatalog.Root/components/alert">alert</a>).</p>

<h2 id="accessibility">Accessibility</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Every control has a visible <code>&lt;label&gt;</code> tied with <code>for</code> (or a visually hidden one, <code>sr-only</code>).</li>
    <li>Errors are linked to their control (<a href="@UiDocsCatalog.Root/components/field#accessibility">field</a>); the validation summary announces itself with <code>role="alert"</code>.</li>
    <li>Group related radios and checkboxes in a <a href="@UiDocsCatalog.Root/components/fieldset">fieldset</a> with a legend.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="guidelines">Guidelines</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Do post and redirect (PRG); give destructive forms <code>data-confirm</code>.</li>
    <li>Do order the actions secondary first, primary last, and keep one primary button per form.</li>
    <li>Don't use <code>asp-validation-summary</code> - its empty state renders an inline style the Content Security Policy blocks; use <code>&lt;dnf-validation-summary /&gt;</code>.</li>
</ul>
